1
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:05,799
Therese, a student on approved leave, signs in to come back.

2
00:00:06,799 --> 00:00:12,800
The Readmission page: enrollment stays closed until readmission is approved. The leave being ended is pre-filled.

3
00:00:13,699 --> 00:00:18,699
The rule: a returning student writes an intent to enroll, Handbook page fifty-three.

4
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:27,100
Therese picks the return semester, gives a reason, and confirms the four checklist items.

5
00:00:30,899 --> 00:00:34,399
Submitted, to Graduate School staff and then the Dean.

6
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:37,000
Graduate School staff signs in.

7
00:00:39,299 --> 00:00:45,299
The Readmission board has the same layout with its own columns. Therese's card is in Submitted.

8
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:54,599
The request shows the return semester, the intention, and the linked leave.

9
00:00:54,799 --> 00:01:00,500
The checklist shows what the student ticked, not yet verified, and the leave history.

10
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:07,500
The policy check flags an early return. Only the Dean can allow that, so it shows Needs review.

11
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:19,000
Forwarding, Graduate School staff ticks the items verified. Anything unticked reaches the Dean as Needs review.

12
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,399
The Dean signs in to decide.

13
00:01:31,799 --> 00:01:36,700
The Dean approves the return, with a note.

14
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:43,599
Therese is active again. Readmission restores standing but does not enroll subjects. The Academic Coordinator does that next.

15
00:01:44,299 --> 00:01:50,299
Graduate School staff signs in.

16
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:56,799
The staff board now shows the Academic Coordinator as next owner, flagged for the Registrar.

17
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,700
The same Registrar list: download, send, mark sent, then acknowledged.

18
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:06,799
Therese signs back in.

19
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,700
Therese sees the approval, with messages from staff and the Dean.
